==English==
[[Image:Amaryllis_belladonna_sfbg_1.jpg|thumb|right|200px|{{taxlink|Amaryllis belladonna|species}}]]

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|-}} {{m|mul|Amaryllis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌæməˈɹɪlɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|amaryllises|amaryllides|pl2qual=obsolete}}

# A {{vern|belladonna lily}} ({{taxlink|Amaryllis belladonna|species}}), native to South Africa.
# A similar lily in genus {{taxfmt|Hippeastrum|genus}}, such as {{taxlink|Hippeastrum puniceum|species}}, and cultivars.

====Usage notes====
The plural {{m|en|amaryllides}} also exists, but is obsolete.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Amaryllis belladona}} {{vern|belladonna lily}}, {{vern|naked-lady-lily}}, {{vern|Jersey lily}}; {{vern|March lily}} {{qualifier|South Africa}}

